<title>ISRAEL: ECI, BT deal worth over $58 mln.</title>
<headline>ECI, BT deal worth over $58 mln.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>ECI Telecom Ltd said it has been chosen by British Telecom as a major supplier of its DACS-2 pair gain systems in a three-year framework agreement valued at over $58 million.</p>
<p>The Israeli company's systems will be employed within BT's networks as primary lines, using copper infrastructure. The DACS-2 enable a single copper twisted pair to carry two digital lines simultaneously.</p>
<p>- Tel  Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
